// Source: Cpp1 `throw;` inside a handler, mistakenly ported as `throw()`,
// and a Cpp1 `throw a, b;` comma expression. functions.md: `throw(x)` needs
// parentheses around the one thrown value; `throw;` rethrows.
// expect-error: 'throw()' has no value: use 'throw(value)', or 'throw;' to rethrow the exception being handled
// expect-error: 'throw' takes one value: use 'throw(value)'
main: () = {
    try {
        throw(1);
    }
    catch (_) {
        throw();
    }
    throw(1, 2);
}
